 # HUMAN RESOURCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (HRMS)
        ## REQUIREMENTS ORGANIZED BY ROLE AND SUBSYSTEM

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: CANDIDATE/NEW HIRE
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Setup & Task Management
        **Requirements:**
        1. Document Upload & Process Initiation
           - **User Stories:**
             - As a Candidate, I want to upload signed contract and candidate required forms and templates to initiate the onboarding process.
           - **Business Rules:** (Not specified in requirements)
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None (Configuration)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - New Hire Tracker (ONB-004)

        2. Onboarding Tracker Access
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-004: As a New Hire, I want to view my onboarding steps in a tracker, so that I know what to complete next.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 11(a, b): The orientation program must include an onboarding workflow and support department-specific tasks and training plans
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None (Onboarding Checklist Data)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Notifications (N)

        3. Onboarding Reminders
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-005: As a New Hire, I want to receive reminders and notifications, so that I don't miss important onboarding tasks.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 12: The system must support sending reminders and task assignments to responsible parties, and track delivery and status accordingly
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Notifications Module (N)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:** None

        ### Subsystem: Document Management & Compliance
        **Requirements:**
        4. Compliance Document Upload
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-007: As a New Hire, I want to upload documents (e.g., ID, contracts, certifications), so that compliance is ensured.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 7: Documents must be collected and verified by the HR department before the first working day
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None (New Hire Input)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Employee Profile (EP)

        **Actions/Processes:**
        9. Compliance & Tracking
           - **Actor:** New Hire
           - **Process:** View onboarding tracker [ONB-004]; receive reminders [ONB-005]; upload compliance documents [ONB-007]
           - **Supporting:**
             - ONB-004: View onboarding steps in tracker
             - ONB-005: Receive reminders and notifications
             - ONB-007: Upload compliance documents
             - BR: Tracker and reminders required; documents stored securely
           - **Output:** Documents Uploaded (Stored); Task Progress Updated
           - **Data Flow:** Documents stored in Employee Profile

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: HR MANAGER
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Setup & Task Management
        **Requirements:**
        5. Onboarding Checklist Creation
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-001: As an HR Manager, I want to create onboarding task checklists, so that new hires complete all required steps.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 8
             - BR 11
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None (Configuration)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - New Hire Tracker (ONB-004)

        6. Employee Profile Creation
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-002: As an HR Manager, I want to be able to access signed contract detail to be able create an employee profile.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 17(a, b)
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Recruitment: Signed Offer Letter/Contract
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Employee Profile (EP)

        ### Subsystem: Access, Resources & Provisioning
        **Requirements:**
        7. Automated Account Provisioning
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-013: As a HR Manager, I want automated account provisioning (SSO/email/tools) on start date and scheduled revocation on exit, so access is consistent and secure.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 9(b): IT (allocation of email, laptop, system access) is an automated task
             - BR 20: The system should allow onboarding cancellation/termination of the created employee profile in case of a "no show"
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - System Admin Configuration
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - IT/Access Systems, Offboarding

        ### Subsystem: Payroll & Benefits Initiation
        **Requirements:**
        8. Payroll Initiation
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-018: As a HR Manager, I want the system to automatically handle payroll initiation based on the contract signing day for the current payroll cycle.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 9(a): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for HR (payroll & benefits' creation). This relates to the Payroll requirement REQ-PY-23 to automatically process payroll initiation
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Recruitment: Contract Signing Date
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Payroll Module (PY)

        9. Signing Bonus Processing
           - **User Stories:**
             - ONB-019: As a HR Manager, I want the system to automatically process signing bonuses based on contract after a new hire is signed.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 9(a): This relates to the Payroll requirement REQ-PY-27 to automatically process signing bonuses
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Recruitment: Contract Details
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Payroll Module (PY)

        **Actions/Processes:**
        8. Profile Creation & Checklist
           - **Actor:** HR Manager
           - **Process:** Create onboarding task checklists [ONB-001]; access signed contract to create employee profile [ONB-002]
           - **Supporting:**
             - ONB-001: Create onboarding task checklists
             - ONB-002: Access signed contract to create employee profile
             - BR: Triggered by offer acceptance; checklists customizable
           - **Output:** Employee Profile (Active); Onboarding Checklist (Activated)
           - **Data Flow:** Uses signed contract data from Recruitment; outputs to Employee Profile

        11. Payroll Initiation & Benefits
           - **Actor:** HR Manager
           - **Process:** Automate payroll initiation upon contract signing [ONB-018]; process signing bonuses [ONB-019]
           - **Supporting:**
             - ONB-018: Automatically handle payroll initiation based on contract signing
             - ONB-019: Automatically process signing bonuses
             - BR: Bonuses treated as distinct payroll components; payroll trigger automatic
           - **Output:** Payroll Initiation Triggered; Bonus Processed
           - **Data Flow:** Triggers payroll processing steps (REQ-PY-23, REQ-PY-27)

        12. Scheduled Access Management
           - **Actor:** HR Manager / System Admin
           - **Process:** Schedule automatic provisioning and revocation of accounts [ONB-013]
           - **Supporting:**
             - ONB-013: Automated account provisioning on start date and scheduled revocation on exit
             - BR: Provisioning and security must be consistent
           - **Output:** Scheduled Revocation Flag
           - **Data Flow:** Info passed to Offboarding (OFF-007) for security control

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: SYSTEM ADMIN
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Access, Resources & Provisioning
        **Requirements:**
        10. System Access Provisioning
            - **User Stories:**
              - ONB-009: As a System Admin, I want to provision system access (payroll, email, internal systems), so that the employee can work.
            - **Business Rules:**
              - BR 9(b): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for IT (allocation of email, laptop, system access)
            - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
              - Employee Profile: New Hire Record
            - **Downstream Dependencies:**
              - Notifications (N) to IT/Access Systems, Payroll

        **Actions/Processes:**
        10. Resource Provisioning
            - **Actor:** HR Employee / System Admin
            - **Process:** Reserve and track equipment [ONB-012]; provision secure system access [ONB-009]
            - **Supporting:**
              - ONB-012: Reserve and track equipment
              - ONB-009: Provision system access
              - BR: IT and payroll access automated; all resources tracked
            - **Output:** Access Granted; Equipment Reserved
            - **Data Flow:** Logged for audit; feeds Time Management (clock access)

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: HR EMPLOYEE
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Access, Resources & Provisioning
        **Requirements:**
        11. Equipment & Resource Reservation
            - **User Stories:**
              - ONB-012: As a HR Employee, I want to reserve and track equipment, desk and access cards for new hires, so resources are ready on Day 1.
            - **Business Rules:**
              - BR 9(c): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for Admin (allocation and assignment of workspace, ID badge)
            - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None
            - **Downstream Dependencies:**
              - Notifications (N) to Facilities/Admin Systems

        ## ====================
        ## ONBOARDING PROCESS WORKFLOW
        ## ====================

        **Phase 2: Onboarding (Integration & Provisioning)**
        1. **Setup & Checklist:** HR Manager creates onboarding task checklists [ONB-001]
        2. **Profile Creation:** HR Manager accesses signed contract to create employee profile [ONB-002]
        3. **Document Collection:** New Hire uploads compliance documents [ONB-007]
        4. **Resource Reservation:** HR Employee reserves equipment, desk, access cards [ONB-012]
        5. **System Access:**
           - System Admin provisions system access [ONB-009]
           - HR Manager ensures automated account provisioning [ONB-013]
        6. **New Hire Tracking:**
           - New Hire views onboarding steps in tracker [ONB-004]
           - New Hire receives reminders [ONB-005]
        7. **Payroll Initiation:**
           - System automatically handles payroll initiation [ONB-018]
           - System automatically processes signing bonuses [ONB-019]

        ## ====================
        ## ONBOARDING BUSINESS RULES SUMMARY
        ## ====================

        **Complete List of Business Rules:**
        - BR 7: Documents must be collected and verified by the HR department before the first working day
        - BR 8: (Not detailed in requirements but referenced)
        - BR 9(a): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for HR (payroll & benefits' creation)
        - BR 9(b): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for IT (allocation of email, laptop, system access)
        - BR 9(c): Auto onboarding tasks are generated for Admin (allocation and assignment of workspace, ID badge)
        - BR 11: (Not detailed in requirements but referenced)
        - BR 11(a, b): The orientation program must include an onboarding workflow and support department-specific tasks and training plans
        - BR 12: The system must support sending reminders and task assignments to responsible parties, and track delivery and status accordingly
        - BR 17(a, b): (Not detailed in requirements but referenced)
        - BR 20: The system should allow onboarding cancellation/termination of the created employee profile in case of a "no show"

        **Related Payroll Business Rules:**
        - REQ-PY-23: Automatically process payroll initiation
        - REQ-PY-27: Automatically process signing bonuses



        # HUMAN RESOURCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (HRMS)
        ## REQUIREMENTS ORGANIZED BY ROLE AND SUBSYSTEM

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: EMPLOYEE
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Termination & Resignation Initiation
        **Requirements:**
        1. Resignation Request Submission
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-018: As an Employee, I want to be able to request a Resignation request with reasoning.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 6: Employee separation can be triggered by resignation. A clearly identified offboarding approval workflow should be identified (e.g., Employee resigning > Line Manager > Financial approval > HR processing/approval)
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Employee Profile: Resignation Reason
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Offboarding Approval Workflow

        2. Resignation Status Tracking
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-019: As an Employee, I want to be able to track my resignation request status.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 6: Employee separation can be triggered by resignation. A clearly identified offboarding approval workflow should be identified
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Employee Profile: Resignation Reason
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Offboarding Approval Workflow

        **Actions/Processes:**
        13. Exit Initiation
           - **Actor:** Employee / HR Manager
           - **Process:** Employee submits resignation [OFF-018] or HR initiates termination review [OFF-001]
           - **Supporting:**
             - OFF-018: Employee requests resignation with reasoning
             - OFF-019: Employee tracks resignation request status
             - OFF-001: HR initiates termination review based on warnings/performance
             - BR: Separation may result from resignation or termination; justification mandatory
           - **Output:** Resignation Request Submitted; Termination Review Started
           - **Data Flow:** Status triggers workflow approval

        ## ====================
        ## ROLE: HR MANAGER
        ## ====================

        ### Subsystem: Termination & Resignation Initiation
        **Requirements:**
        3. Termination Review Initiation
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-001: As an HR Manager, I want to initiate termination reviews based on warnings and performance data / manager requests, so that exits are justified.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 4: Employee separation needs an effective date and a clearly stated and identified reason for exit. Termination reviews based on performance must follow due process
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Performance Management (PM): Warnings/Low Scores
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Offboarding Approval Workflow

        ### Subsystem: Clearance, Handover & Access Revocation
        **Requirements:**
        4. Offboarding Checklist Management
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-006: As an HR Manager, I want an offboarding checklist (IT assets, ID cards, equipment), so no company property is lost.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 13(a): (Clearance checklist requirement - not fully detailed in provided text)
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:** None (Configuration)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Clearance Workflow (OFF-010)

        5. Multi-Department Exit Clearance
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-010: As HR Manager, I want multi-department exit clearance sign-offs (IT, Finance, Facilities, Line Manager), with statuses, so the employee is fully cleared.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 13(b, c): Clearance checklist required across departments (IT, HR, Admin, Finance). Final approvals/signature form should be filed to HR to complete the offboarding process
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Clearance Status Updates (from Departments)
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Payroll: Final Settlement

        ### Subsystem: Exit Settlements & Benefits
        **Requirements:**
        6. Final Settlement Trigger
           - **User Stories:**
             - OFF-013: As HR Manager, I want to send offboarding notification to trigger benefits termination and final pay calc (unused leave, deductions), so settlements are accurate.
           - **Business Rules:**
             - BR 9: (Not detailed in provided text but referenced)
             - BR 11: Leaves' Balance must be reviewed and settled (unused annuals to be encashed). Benefits plans are set to be auto-terminated as of the end of the notice period
           - **Inputs from Other Sub-Systems:**
             - Leaves Module: Balance
             - Employee Profile: Benefits
           - **Downstream Dependencies:**
             - Payroll Module (PY)

        **Actions/Processes:**
        13. Exit Initiation (Partial)
           - **Actor:** HR Manager
           - **Process:** HR initiates termination review [OFF-001] based on warnings and performance data/manager requests
           - **Supporting:**
             - OFF-001: Initiate termination reviews
             - BR 4: Termination reviews based on performance must follow due process
           - **Output:** Termination Review Started

        14. Clearance & Assets
           - **Actor:** HR Manager
           - **Process:** Manage offboarding checklist and departmental sign-offs (IT, Finance, Facilities, etc.) [OFF-006, OFF-010]
           - **Supporting:**
             - OFF-006: Offboarding checklist for asset recovery
             - OFF-010: Multi-department exit clearance sign-offs
             - BR: Multi-department clearance required; completion tracked
           - **Output:** Offboarding Checklist Active; Clearance Sign-offs Logged
           - **Data Flow:** Clearance governs final payroll release

        16. Final Settlement
           - **Actor:** HR Manager
           - **Process:** Trigger final pay calculation and benefits termination [OFF-013]
           - **Supporting:**
             - OFF-013: Trigger benefits termination and final pay calculation
             - BR: Final pay includes unused leave, deductions, loans, severance; benefits auto-terminate
           - **Output:** Final Pay Calculation Triggered; Benefits Termination Scheduled
           - **Data Flow:** Sends encashment data from Leaves; triggers Payroll processing

